                        question: "What is npm?",
                        answer:
                        "npm, commonly known as the Node Package Manager, is a package manager and registry commonly used with Node.js projects. It allows developers to install, update, remove, and manage third-party packages and project dependencies. It also provides scripts for automating common project tasks."
