                        question: "What is DNS caching and TTL?",

                        answer:
                        "DNS caching stores DNS query results temporarily so that repeated lookups can be answered more quickly and with less traffic. TTL, or Time To Live, specifies how long a DNS record may be cached before it should be queried again. A shorter TTL can allow changes to propagate more quickly but may increase DNS query traffic."
