                        question: "What are the types of polymorphism in Java?",

                        answer:
                        "The commonly discussed types are compile-time polymorphism and runtime polymorphism. Compile-time polymorphism is primarily achieved through method overloading, where the compiler selects the applicable method. Runtime polymorphism is achieved through method overriding, where the JVM selects the overridden instance method based on the actual object."
