                        "Black Box Testing is performed with little or no prior knowledge of the target environment and simulates an external attacker with limited information. White Box Testing is performed with extensive information about the target, such as architecture, source code, credentials, or configuration details, allowing a deeper assessment. Grey Box Testing combines elements of both approaches by providing the tester with limited or partial information."
